8. Interview questions
Q1. What is Named Entity Recognition?
NER is an NLP task that identifies entity mentions in text and classifies them into categories such as person, organization, date, and money.
Q2. What is the difference between NER and text classification?
NER identifies and labels specific spans within text, while text classification assigns a category to a larger piece of text.
Q3. Can NER identify multiple-word names?
Yes. It can recognize spans such as HDFC Bank or Arun Kumar.
Q4. Is NER used in RAG applications?
It can be. NER may extract metadata from documents, improve filtering, or support structured retrieval. However, a RAG system does not always need NER.
Q5. Does NER verify extracted information?
No. It identifies and classifies text spans; separate validation or verification is needed to establish factual correctness.
